WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.980
APIs are interfaces that expose data, business logic, automation, and service-to-service communication.

2
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:19.080
A Python API might support a customer portal, a mobile application, an internal operations tool, a partner integration, a batch workflow, or an automation endpoint used by other services.

3
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:29.980
The interface may not have a traditional browser screen, but it still makes decisions about identity, data access, workflow state, and sensitive operations.

4
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:35.300
API security with Python means protecting the full request and response lifecycle.

5
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:53.880
That includes route design, request validation, authentication, authorization, token handling, object-level access control, data access, file handling, secrets, dependencies, logging, monitoring, and deployment assumptions.

6
00:00:53.980 --> 00:01:03.740
Frameworks such as Flask, Django, and FastAPI can provide useful patterns, but the application still owns its trust boundaries and business rules.

7
00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.420
It helps to separate the layers involved.

8
00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:09.720
API design defines what clients can ask for.

9
00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:12.780
Application logic decides what the system should do.

10
00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.480
Identity systems establish who or what is calling.

11
00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:19.940
Authorization determines whether the caller may perform the action.

12
00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:26.520
Infrastructure may provide gateways, proxies, TLS, routing, and rate controls.

13
00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:32.220
Operations teams provide logging, alerting, patching, and incident response.

14
00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.840
Secure APIs require these layers to reinforce one another.

15
00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:41.880
The safest API programs have clear ownership, documentation, tests, and monitoring.

16
00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:53.100
Every endpoint should have a purpose, an expected caller, an input contract, an authorization model, a response contract, and operational signals that show whether it is behaving normally.

17
00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:56.960
API security is not a one-time gate before launch.

18
00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:02.980
It is a continuous discipline across design, implementation, deployment, and production review.
